"answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative launched by Zenith Aerospace Inc. The project kicked off on June 15th with a $500,000 budget for phase one, led by Sarah Tan. The team expanded to include five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, with onboarding on September 10th, and later welcomed Mike Chen (machine learning) and Lisa Ray (cloud computing). A call for ideas regarding AI-enhanced data visualization was issued by July 20th. The project successfully completed its design phase and reached its first major milestone ahead of schedule with a tested secure file sharing prototype. The next phase involves user interface enhancements starting in October, followed by a development phase led by Omar Jensen. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought by the end of November. Security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest, will be updated effective January next year. Additionally, a $15,000 training budget has been approved for the coding team and project managers, with sessions starting next month."
